    {
      "source": "D811-D813/D818/P121-P126",
      "fact": "The magnet expected geometry was fixed independently from the actual source/work area/DPI and default10/16DIP parameters, without calling the product solver for the oracle. One new blank target of the exact Run/Medium process was created and identity-bound; fixture SetWindowPos set up only that newly owned target. The source remained the real Terminal. Target relationships did not grant authority."
    },
    {
      "source": "D822/D825/D828/D831/P128/P131/P133/P134",
      "fact": "Generation4 actually completed free movement, XY snap, holding outside the entry threshold but inside release, and detach, with exact source geometry and unchanged target. Free/XY/detach each had one actual successful exact native placement. Hold was an actual consumed placement receipt with already_exact_no_native_call/native_attempted=false, not a new API attempt or failure."
    },
    {
      "source": "D829-D835",
      "fact": "Before a Resnap packet was recorded, TEST reported geometry_TEST_phase_one_shot_wait_failed. No actual failing branch, notification count or cap-exceeded receipt exists in this run. A source-level cumulative64-notification hypothesis is not an observed native cause. Five-phase completion and Ctrl were not reached; original driverFAIL is preserved."
