    {
      "source": "D832/P136/P138/P141/P143-P146",
      "fact": "After the test failure only its cleanup LEFTUP was inserted. Product really observed matching Raw UP and accepted legacy UP, successfully released capture and detached, then recorded winevent_foreground with foreground66188/source131926 and ended generation4 as FocusLost/end2/normal_up=false. Gone reported release/detach/destroy/hotkey cleanup. A cleanup UP or accepted legacy UP must not be converted into the planned NormalUp; the foreground origin does not identify the initiating process or system root cause."
    },
    {
      "source": "D833-D848/P150",
      "fact": "Normal WM_CLOSE was attempted once on the exact Terminal but root-gone was not confirmed; actual wait258/exit259 remain. The blank target's own DestroyWindow/UnregisterClass succeeded. Public same-EXE --quit actually signalled product exit0; P150 reports own hooks/overlay/native worker/input/capture/association/visual recovery stopped and no completion unknown. Independent owner retired the lease and actually switched/read back Default with handles closed. Aggregate cleanup_known=false and original UNKNOWN/BLOCKED summaries remain, despite those separately positive facts."
    },
    {
      "source": "D851-D858/collection and cleanup receipts",
      "fact": "The new Shell child was still alive, left to the exact guest job/disposal; desktop-object destruction and complete application-tree normal exit were not proven. Driver exited1 with one live descendant and forced test cleanup. Stable evidence collection and later exact guest/task cleanup preserved hashes; guest disposal is not product or whole-chain cleanup PASS."
